s-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:9b6cac3b6f2c432a82fe8c1d18bcae7796315cf16b89072c81a72d52e83aa080","file":"preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-Ising-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/sections/extensions.tex","line":245,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"f9b89713255095df70e2a51c3839fe1bfe0732f63e814b656446a3d2e6b27fd8","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-Ising-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/sections/extensions.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:9b6cac3b6f2c432a82fe8c1d18bcae7796315cf16b89072c81a72d52e83aa080","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/The-free-energy-of-the-Ising-random-perceptron-September-24-2026/build/sections/extensions.tex#L245"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{ext:sign}\nReplace the Gaussian pattern entries by independent uniform signs in\n$\\{-1,1\\}$. If $f$ is bounded Borel and its discontinuity set has Gaussian\nmeasure zero, then its expected pressure and its pressure in probability\nconverge to the same value $\\mathcal P_f(\\alpha)$ as in\nTheorem~\\ref{thm:main}. In particular, this holds for every bounded\ncontinuous activation."}
